	regionKind = "city",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Thunder Bluff is the capital of the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, raised on a cluster of windswept mesas that tower hundreds of feet above the plains of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}. Bridges of wood and rope swing between the heights, and every mesa is crowned with tents, longhouses, painted totems and spirit lodges. Great lifts of rope and timber carry travellers up from the grass below, and wind riders circle the central tower. It is a city of many tribes and a refuge for hunters, traders and artisans of every kind. From his lodge on the central mesa, the High Chieftain {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} watches over all of them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[For countless generations the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} had no city. They were nomads, and the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} hunted them across the plains until their tribes were few and scattered. {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} of the Bloodhoof dreamed of a land where his people could live in peace. With the help of {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} and the orcs of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, the tauren drove the centaur out of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}. On the mesas at its northern end Cairne built a refuge where tauren of every tribe would be welcome. No chronicle records the year it was finished. Over time the scattered tribes came to it and united under his rule.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} is old, but his strength and wisdom still hold the tribes together. Not every tribe agrees with the path he has chosen. On {link:elder-rise}Elder Rise{/link}, {link:magatha-grimtotem}Magatha Grimtotem{/link}, the Elder Crone of {link:grimtotem-clan}the Grimtotem{/link}, keeps her own counsel and her own guards, and she believes that she, not Cairne, should lead the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}. Beside her the druids of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link} tend their lodges under {link:hamuul-runetotem}Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem{/link}. Emissaries of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} dwell in the {link:the-pools-of-vision}Pools of Vision{/link} and teach on {link:spirit-rise}Spirit Rise{/link}, a sign of the pact that brought them into the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. The sages of the city are known across the Horde as historians. In these days new faces have come as well: priests of An'she, the sun, and {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} elves who pass through on their way from the camp of the {link:earthen-ring}Earthen Ring{/link} to {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of many tribes.{/b} The Bloodhoof, the Runetotem, the Wildmane, the Thunderhorn, the Ragetotem, the Stonehoof, the Mistrunner and many others keep their trades on the rises.
• {b}The Grimtotem.{/b} {link:magatha-grimtotem}Magatha{/link} and her servants hold a corner of {link:elder-rise}Elder Rise{/link}.
• {b}The druids.{/b} Tauren of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link}, led by {link:hamuul-runetotem}Hamuul Runetotem{/link}.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Apothecaries, priests and mages sent from the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}.
• {b}Travellers of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link}, trolls and now {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} come and go by wind rider and lift.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Long March.{/b} {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s orcs escorted {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link}'s people across {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link} to {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}, and Cairne pledged the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} to the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} Tauren warriors fought beside the orcs, the humans and the night elves at the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}.
• {b}The Founding.{/b} With the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} driven off, Cairne raised Thunder Bluff and called the tribes to it.
• {b}The Pact with the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} When the Forsaken sought a place in the Horde, the elders of the {link:earthen-ring}Earthen Ring{/link} urged that they be helped. Cairne agreed, and the Forsaken came to Thunder Bluff as allies.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Bluffs",
			text = [=[• The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} keep a custom of scattering incense to the winds from the southern cliff of {link:hunter-rise}Hunter Rise{/link}.
• A young tauren who stands before the High Chieftain wears a headdress, and the finest are made with {link:harpies}harpy{/link} feathers from the north.
• The sages of Thunder Bluff have studied metal discs brought back from {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link}, whose glyphs speak of a lost place called {link:valley-of-the-watchers}Uldum{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

